  "pipeline_stage": "validated",
  "title": "Motor imagination and execution with a chronic wireless epidural ECoG BCI (WIMAGINE), one participant with tetraplegia (Pollina et al. 2026)",
  "description": "Band-pass filtered (1-250 Hz) epidural ECoG recordings from one participant with incomplete C6 tetraplegia, chronically implanted with the WIMAGINE wireless device. The participant executed or imagined right-arm reaching and wrist-extension movements, alone or simultaneously (one executed, one imagined), across eight sessions with EMG monitoring. The data accompany a study of how simultaneous motor imagination and execution are decoupled through orthogonal neural representations. This is a BIDS derivative repackaging of the authors' Zenodo release.",
  "methods_description": "32 channels of the left WIMAGINE epidural implant over primary motor and sensory cortex were recorded at about 585 Hz. The implant applied an analog 0.5-300 Hz band-pass and a 292.8 Hz FIR low-pass. The authors then applied a zero-phase 5th-order Butterworth 1-250 Hz band-pass. The seated participant followed on-screen instructions to execute or imagine reaching and wrist-extension movements. EMG of the extensor digitorum and lateral deltoid monitored execution.",
